H9 amxmodx_mm.dll -- AMX Mod X's core (a Metamod plugin), built from source for 128 player slots
================================================================================================

What this is
------------

ts\addons\amxmodx\dlls\amxmodx_mm.dll is AMX Mod X's core (a Metamod plugin),
built by H9 from TSM\AMXMODX: goldsrc-net/amxmodx (the AMX Mod X fork reTS ships with),
branch 64bit at commit dedff660dff3fa615a96d6ba3890d6000b588ed1,
with H9's changes as uncommitted working-tree changes (AMXMODX\H9-SOURCE.txt).
The core and every module H9 ships but three are built together from that one tree, for
128 player slots: tsx_amxx.dll stays reTSX (docs\PLAYER_LIMIT_128.txt, section 8.5),
easy_http_amxx.dll is a third-party module, and mysql_amxx.dll (it links MySQL's C
connector, and no H9 plugin loads it) stays the release's.

H9's changes in it
------------------

  amxmodx\amxmodx.h, meta_api.cpp
          AMXX_MAX_PLAYERS 128: the core keeps a CPlayer for edict 1 to 128
          (g_players[AMXX_MAX_PLAYERS + 1]; upstream g_players[33]). Every look-up
          is still bounded by the server's maxplayers.
  amxmodx\emsg.cpp
          DeathMsg's killer and victim are taken up to maxplayers (and 128) instead
          of up to 32, so kills past slot 32 reach client_death and the stats.
  plugins\include\amxconst.inc
          MAX_PLAYERS 128, deployed with this core to scripting\include: H9's
          plugins (build.bat) are compiled against it.
  amxmodx\meta_api.cpp
          client_disconnected and client_remove fire from the game's ClientDisconnect
          whenever no SV_DropClient hook saw the leave first: on Xash3D, which has
          no hook for the core (no ReHLDS API, no gamedata signature), every leave,
          with drop false and no message. Upstream fired neither there, and logged
          "client_disconnected and client_remove forwards have been disabled"; the
          core now logs "No SV_DropClient hook (...): ... fire from ClientDisconnect".

