Against the build it replaces
-----------------------------

The amxmodx_mm.dll H9 shipped before, from the reTS AMX Mod X build (1.10.0-manual):
1964544 bytes, SHA256 69F648702AAB829BF6E9F5617082FB50D1B099C9390FF32823FB520C04446594,
kept as amxmodx_mm.dll.bak_slots beside this file. To go back, copy that over amxmodx_mm.dll.

On servers of 32 slots or fewer nothing changes: the tables are longer, and every loop and
bound in them still stops at the server's maxplayers.

Past 32 slots
-------------

This core is safe past 32; AMX Mod X as a whole is not yet. A server past 32 slots runs
with AMX Mod X loaded only once both of these are done too:
  * tsx_amxx.dll: reTSX is built for 32 slots. The TSX it extends keeps 33-entry
    player tables, indexed by edict number up to maxplayers, so a player in slot 33
    or up is written past them. TS 3.0's TSX in this tree is built for 128 but has
    no reTS backend (docs\PLAYER_LIMIT_128.txt, section 8.5).
  * The stock plugins (admin.amxx and the rest) are the release's, compiled for
    MAX_PLAYERS 32: get_players() writes one cell per player into their 32-cell
    buffers. They need compiling against this amxconst.inc.
